5. Ensure the preview re-renders on all relevant content changes (text body, title, media embeds, custom blocks) by subscribing to the same content store or state slice the editor uses.

6. Add a toggle control (button or switch) in the editor toolbar to show/hide the live preview pane; persist the user's preference in local storage or user settings.

7. Handle edge cases: empty content state (show placeholder text), very large content (throttle or virtualize if needed), and unsupported block types (render a fallback message).

